sentences.l:
Take your-guard from her-glance, for-it (is) a-sorcerer, * and-not (is) escaping (he) whom have-shot-him the-eye-hollows;
and-not deceive from a-softness in her-speech, * for-indeed the-wine to-the-minds steals-in.
Delicately-reared: if touched the-rose her-cheek, * she-would-weep, and-would-flow from its-two-eyes the-rains;
and-if in the-slumber passed the-breeze by-her-land, * it-would-travel ever from her-land, and-it (is) fragrant.
Her-necklaces complain (of the) ringing (of) her-sash, * and-indeed have-gone-dumb from her-two-wrists the-bracelets.
My-reproacher, may-God-strip-you, not you (are) fair! * For-from (the) beauty (of) this the-gazelle are-turned-back the-gazes.

sentences.i:
Beware of her glance, for it is a sorcerer, * and none escapes whom those eyes have shot;
do not be beguiled by the softness of her speech, * for wine steals into the mind unawares.
So tender is she that if a rose but brushed her cheek, * she would weep, and rain would pour from its eyes;
if the breeze passed by her country in the night’s slumber, * it would go on from her country fragrant for ever.
Her necklaces complain of the chiming of her sash, * while on her wrists the bracelets are struck dumb.
You who blame me, God strip you bare, you are not fair: * from the beauty of this gazelle all eyes are turned back.

sentences.l:
You-made-good your-opinion of-the-days when they-were-good, * and-not you-feared (the) evil (of) what brings it the-fate;
and-made-peace-with-you the-nights, so-you-were-deceived by-them, * and-at (the) clearness (of) the-nights happens the-muddiness.
O company (of) the-people, whoever, was the-Time to-him * a-helper, then-let-be of his-judgment the-caution.

sentences.i:
You thought well of the days while they went well, * and did not fear the harm that fate brings with it;
the nights kept the peace with you, and you were lulled by them, * yet when the nights run clearest the mud is stirred.
O you people, whoever finds that Time is on his side, * let caution be part of his counsel.
